# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — the AZURE/RELEASE variant.
#
# The development repository excluded every generated artefact, on the principle
# that a result in the tree which disagrees with the current code is worse than
# no result at all. This copy inverts that for one specific reason: it exists to
# be CLONED ONTO A FRESH MACHINE AND REPRODUCED, and a clone that arrives without
# the retrieved corpus cannot be reproduced at all — the publisher endpoints that
# served those 69 manuscripts return 403 non-deterministically.
#
# So the inputs and the published artefacts are TRACKED here, and `reference/`
# keeps an immutable checksummed copy of the latter. What stays ignored is what
# is genuinely scratch: run directories, logs, caches, the venv.
# =============================================================================

# --- genuinely regenerable scratch -------------------------------------------
# ~30 files per calculation, hundreds of MB. The scientific record is the .fdf
# settings, and those are recorded inside each verdict in data/processed/verification/.
data/interim/siesta_runs/
data/interim/corpus_terms/
logs/*.log
logs/setup/
*.log

# --- environment and secrets --------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
opt/

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- siesta run artefacts loose in the tree -----------------------------------
*.XV
*.DM
*.HSX
*.bands
submit/

# --- latex --------------------------------------------------------------------
manuscript/build/
manuscript/*.aux
manuscript/*.fls
manuscript/*.fdb_latexmk
manuscript/*.blg
manuscript/*.synctex.gz
manuscript/References_pdf/

# --- development snapshots ----------------------------------------------------
backup/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
